From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:10:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 436/488] [DS4.1] Top-k and top-p filtering in TileLang

The V2 runner's top-k / top-p filtering ran apply_top_k_top_p_triton's
four Triton kernels: the monolithic top-k/top-p kernel and the split
top-p pipeline (stats, five pivot-search steps, mask). Each is now a
TileLang kernel that is its Triton kernel's contract bit for bit, with
the arithmetic read from Triton 3.7's PTX for sm_121a (exp, log, sqrt,
division, the contractions LLVM made, the thread layout by the logits'
16-byte alignment, and the split pipeline's per-lane row sums), launched
as the Triton dispatch does on CUDA and on its buffers. The V2 runner no
longer registers the Triton kernels; the V1 sampler keeps them.
